1
00:00:01,370 --> 00:00:02,490
时间
Time.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:05,060
我们对它总是贪得无厌
We all wish we had more of it.

3
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:08,290
是否有方法能够跳出时间界限
If only there was a way to escape it's bonds.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,020
如我们所愿自由穿行于时间长河
and travel through time as we pleased,

5
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:14,010
回到遥远的过去
Back into the distant past

6
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,020
或者访问几百年后的未来
or hundreds of years into the future.

7
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:21,630
地球上最聪明的大脑致力于此
The greatest minds on earth have spent decades

8
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:26,540
几十年来，屡败屡战
trying to make this dream come true without success.

9
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:30,580
可近来，新的科学透露出
But now new science reveals strange paths

10
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:34,280
通向这个问题终极答案 的怪异之路
that may finally answer the question,

11
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,110
时间旅行可能吗？
is time travel possible?

12
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,820
如果可能，我们怎么才能做到？
And if so,how will we do it?

13
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:50,030
空间，时间，生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,030
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

15
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:59,070
♪穿越虫洞 第1x03集♪
Through the Wormhole 1x03

16
00:00:59,070 --> 00:01:03,070
时间旅行可能吗?
Is Time Travel Possible?

17
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:08,180
某种意义上，地球上的每一个 男人、女人和儿童
in a way,every man,woman,and child on this earth

18
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:09,650
都是时间旅行者
is a time traveler.

19
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:13,850
不管是否愿意，我们都要经历从生到死的旅程
Like it or not,we're all being shot relentlessly forward,

20
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:16,850
持续前行，永不间断
making the journey from birth to death,

21
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:18,890
没有回头路
and there's no going back.

22
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:22,530
无法预知未来
And there's no way of looking into the future.

23
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:25,660
是吗？
Or is there?

24
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:27,970
如果我们能够回到从前
What if we could travel back

25
00:01:27,970 --> 00:01:31,170
见证过去发生的事件
to witness events in the distant past

26
00:01:31,170 --> 00:01:35,570
或者飞向未来，目击自己的命运
or journey into the far future,see our destiny?

27
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:40,650
想想看，我们可以
Just think what we might learn

28
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:44,620
亲眼观察历史
if we could watch history unfold right before our eyes...

29
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:49,750
...或者我们有机会改变
...Or what we could change in our own lives

30
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,860
我们自己的生活
if we had the chance?

31
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:57,860
对多数人来讲，生命中最痛苦的，是失去心中挚爱
For many,life's greatest sorrow is losing a loved one.

32
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:01,270
小时候，与祖母共渡的时光
The time I spent with my grandmother when I was a child

33
00:02:01,270 --> 00:02:04,570
塑造了今天的我
helped make me the man I am today.

34
00:02:04,570 --> 00:02:08,210
我经常希望能够再见到 她老人家
I often wish I could see my grandmother again,

35
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:11,480
或者回到过去，
or go back in time and show her who I am

36
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:14,880
让她看看成年的我
and what I've become as an adult.

37
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:18,480
似乎此梦难圆啊
Seems like an impossible dream.

38
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,850
真的吗？
But is it?

39
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:22,320
科学能够找到
Can science find a way

40
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:26,220
摧毁横亘在现在和未来之间的时间壁垒，的方法吗
to tear down the walls between now and then?

41
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:29,330
时间旅行可能吗？
Is time travel possible?

42
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,060
为了找到答案
To find the answer,

43
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:35,670
我们必须先理解自然的时间
we must first understand the nature of time.

44
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:39,540
这可比听上去难多了
And that's a lot harder than it sounds.

45
00:02:41,810 --> 00:02:47,040
Steve Jefferts是一个原子物理学家 兼大师级计时员
Steve Jefferts is an atomic scientist and master timekeeper.

46
00:02:47,050 --> 00:02:50,050
Jefferts:俺认为，我们所有人
Jefferts:We all,I think,

47
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:53,420
都天生以为自己了解时间
have some innate feeling that we understand time.

48
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:54,720
时间似水，从身边流逝
It flows past us.

49
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,550
韶华易逝
Time goes on,we get older,

50
00:02:56,560 --> 00:03:00,290
故梦难温
things that happened yesterday are not happening today,

51
00:03:00,290 --> 00:03:01,290
等等等等
et cetera.

52
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:03,660
但是我不认为
But I don't think that any of us,

53
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:06,400
有人能够真正理解时间
whether we're physicists who study time

54
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:09,000
无论是我们这些 研究时间的物理学家
or just somebody who lives his life

55
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,100
还是那些打酱油的普通人
really,truly understands time.

56
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,740
弗里曼:Steve供职于
Freeman:Steve works at

57
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:16,770
科罗拉多Boulder的
the National institute of Standards and Technology

58
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,110
国家标准和技术学院
in Boulder,Colorado.

59
00:03:18,110 --> 00:03:20,750
这是世界上6个
It's one of six labs around the world

60
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:23,650
提供宇宙协调时的实验室之一
that calculate coordinated universal time,

61
00:03:23,650 --> 00:03:27,280
宇宙协调时就是世界标准时间
the official world time.

62
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,720
这些激光装置
This tableful of lasers

63
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:33,660
是NIST-F1型铯原子钟
is the NIST-F1 cesium fountain atomic clock.

64
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:36,560
测量原子的振动
Measuring the nuclear vibrations of atoms,

65
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:40,830
每秒钟“滴答”90亿次
this clock ticks at 9 billion times per second.

66
00:03:40,830 --> 00:03:45,070
即1纳秒的十万分之一
That's one ten-millionth of a nanosecond.

67
00:03:45,070 --> 00:03:49,140
这台钟以16位的精度
This clock will measure frequency,or time interval,

68
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:52,610
测试频率，也就是时间间隔
out to almost 16 digits.

69
00:03:52,610 --> 00:03:54,380
这有啥子重要的？
Why is that important?

70
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:58,880
要以如此高的精度 测量时间或者频率的原因是—
The reasons to measure time or frequency this accurately --

71
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:00,990
小子，原因可太多了
boy,there are a bunch of them.

72
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,920
有些是出于纯科学原因，
Some of them are scientific,

73
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,320
还有些可是实际需要
but some of them are really practical.

74
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:07,990
像全球定位系统这样的玩意儿
Systems like the global positioning system,

75
00:04:07,990 --> 00:04:09,130
即GPS系统—
the GPS system --

76
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:11,700
实际上就是一个授时系统—
it's fundamentally a time-keeping system.

77
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:15,100
我们所做的，就是把原子钟 放到那些卫星上去
And so what we do is we put atomic clocks on satellites,

78
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:17,400
确定它们都是同步的
make sure they're all synchronized,

79
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:20,140
这样，当我站在地球表面
and now I stand on the surface of the earth

80
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:21,440
拿着GPS接收器
with my GPS receiver,

81
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:24,540
会收到每个卫星 发来的时间信号
and it gets time signals from each of these satellites,

82
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,910
接收机测量到抵达时刻
and it just measures the arrival times.

83
00:04:26,910 --> 00:04:29,310
如果从那颗卫星来的信号
And so if the signal from that satellite

84
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:33,480
比这颗卫星的信号晚到了5纳秒
arrives five nanoseconds before the signal from that satellite,

85
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:38,190
这说明“哦，我离那颗卫星
it says,"oh,I must be 5 feet further from that satellite

86
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:39,460
比离这颗要远5英尺“
than that satellite."

87
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:42,460
这样，如果有4颗卫星的信号
So it does that with four satellites,

88
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:46,500
接收器就能计算出你所在 的经纬度和海拔了
and it computes your "x" and "y" position and your altitude,

89
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:49,330
你通过时间计算位置
and now you've got your position from time.

90
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:54,340
这个方法很不同寻常，要成功定位
And the fact that this works at all is just remarkable,

91
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:56,010
必须达到纳秒级的
but it absolutely depends on

92
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:58,280
计时精度
having time at the nanosecond level,

93
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:01,480
如果你达不到纳秒级精度
because if you don't have time at the nanosecond level,

94
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:05,320
你就无法区分卫星的远近
then you can't tell which satellite you're closer to.

95
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:13,520
弗里曼:像这样的精确计时，使我们依赖于电脑的
Freeman:Precision timekeeping like this makes our high-tech,

96
00:05:13,530 --> 00:05:17,560
高科技生活方式变得可能
computer-driven lifestyles possible.

97
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:21,700
可是当我们的计时系统 越来越精确
But as our timekeeping systems become ever-more accurate,

98
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:26,000
我们发现时间流逝的方式 和我们的固有观念不同
we find that time does not flow the way we think it does.

99
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,840
时间并不是统一的
Time is not universal.

100
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:34,550
怪异的事实是，时间是个性化的
The strange truth is that time is personal.

101
00:05:34,550 --> 00:05:36,110
时间是什么？
What time is it?

102
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:39,380
呃，这取决于你身处何处
Well,that depends on where you are

103
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:43,550
以及你脚下的大地
and what the ground beneath your feet is doing.

104
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:46,420
当你在一个引力场中 放置一个钟时
Anytime you put a clock in a gravitational field,

105
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:49,930
引力场越强
as you get closer to the strong part of the gravitational field,

106
00:05:49,930 --> 00:05:51,300
钟就会越慢
the clock slows down.

107
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:55,430
事实是，地球并不是 坚固不变的
What ends up happening is that the earth is not rigid.

108
00:05:55,430 --> 00:06:00,240
地球实际上比较柔软，像果冻之类的东西
The earth is sort of a squishy,firm ball of jello or something,

109
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:03,310
每天，当潮起潮落时
and every day,when the tides go in and out,

110
00:06:03,310 --> 00:06:07,280
地球外形也随之变化
the earth deforms sort of like a ball,

111
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:09,410
你脚下的地壳
and the earth under your foot

112
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:12,450
也多多少少的有所升降
goes up and down by a foot more or less --

113
00:06:12,450 --> 00:06:15,290
升降程度各地不同
depends on where on the earth you are.

114
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:18,020
如果我把这个钟拿起来，举高
So if I pick this clock up and move it up by a foot,

115
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:20,290
它离地心远了一点
it's further from the center of the Earth,

116
00:06:20,290 --> 00:06:23,030
引力也小了一些
the gravitational force goes down a little bit,

117
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:26,700
钟摆也会快一点
and the clock ticks a little bit faster.

118
00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:32,500
如果你有一个17位精度的表
So now if you have a clock which is accurate to 17 digits,

119
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:35,310
在一天之中
all of a sudden,every day,

120
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:38,540
你会看到它实际上忽快忽慢
you can see the rate of the clock speed up and slow down

121
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:41,810
因为地球是在变化
and speed up and slow down relative to what it should be,

122
00:06:41,810 --> 00:06:47,420
引力也在变化
because the Earth is squishing by this kind of one-foot level.

123
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:51,260
弗里曼:人类无法察觉这种微小变化
Freeman:Humans don't perceive these miniscule time differences,

124
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:53,160
但是我们最准确的计时器
but our very fastest clocks

125
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:57,830
能够将1秒分为一千兆兆份
can cut a second into a quadrillion pieces.

126
00:06:57,830 --> 00:06:59,460
在这个精度上
And at that scale,

127
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:03,700
我们会看到时间处处不同
we see that time differs from place to place.

128
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:09,440
时间和空间 孟不离焦，焦不离孟
Time and space are tightly locked together.

129
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,340
很快，我们觉悟了
Quickly,we're getting to the point

130
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:13,710
我们开始统一考虑时空
where we're gonna have to start thinking about

131
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:16,180
而不再是时间和空间
space-time together,rather than space and time,

132
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:18,080
这很酷，是吗
which is a cool place to be,right?

133
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:20,680
弗里曼:引力拉慢时间
Freeman:Gravity slows time,

134
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:24,660
这是时间旅行的关键之一
and this is the key to one form of time travel.

135
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:28,530
当你离开一个重力场 比如地球表面
When you leave a gravity field such as the earth's surface,

136
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:32,000
你和你地球上朋友的时间
time moves at a different rate for you

137
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,400
不再相同
than for your friends on earth.

138
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:40,100
你运动的越快 时间差别越大
The time difference is greatest when you move at high speed.

139
00:07:40,110 --> 00:07:44,780
这意味着时间旅行者 身处你我之中
This means that time travelers walk among us.

140
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:49,710
存在时间机器
These are their time machines.

141
00:07:51,450 --> 00:07:57,420
Cosmonaut Sergei Krikalev 是世界上 最伟大的时间旅行者
Cosmonaut Sergei Krikalev is the world's greatest time traveler.

142
00:07:57,420 --> 00:08:03,060
Krikalev以每小时1万7千英里的速度 旅行了803天
Krikalev has spent 803 days moving at 17,000 miles per hour.

143
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:07,160
他在低地球引力的状态下 高速运动
He traveled fast outside earth's gravity,

144
00:08:07,170 --> 00:08:11,700
所以他的时间比 我们的慢的多
so time moved more slowly for him than for us.

145
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:14,610
因为时间流逝的速度不同
Because time passed at different rates,

146
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:17,210
他已经进入未来了—
he has traveled into the future --

147
00:08:17,210 --> 00:08:21,510
1/48秒的未来
1/48 of a second into the future.

148
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:25,280
1/48秒听上去不太刺激
1/48 of a second may not sound like much,

149
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:28,850
但如果他的动力再强点儿 速度再快点儿
but stick more power behind him and make him go faster,

150
00:08:28,850 --> 00:08:33,560
接近光速— 大概每秒30万千米—
near light speed -- about 670 million miles per hour --

151
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:36,960
事情就开始变得怪异了
and things get strange.

152
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,060
如果他以光速旅行1年
If he travels for a year,

153
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:41,330
他回来时会发现
he'll come back and find out

154
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:44,270
他老了12个月
that while he has aged 12 months,

155
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:46,640
地球却老了10岁
earth is 10 years older.

156
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:53,380
这是另一个时间机器
Here is another time machine,

157
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:57,850
它比我们的火箭加速能力还强
and it speeds things up even faster than our rocket ships.

158
00:08:57,850 --> 00:09:03,520
这是欧洲的巨强子对撞机 简称LHC，强壮鸡
It's Europe's Large Hadron Collider,or LHC,

159
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:07,320
世界上最大和最厉害的 粒子加速器
the world's biggest and baddest particle accelerator.

160
00:09:07,330 --> 00:09:10,890
Steve Nahn是麻省理工的 一个物理学教授
Steve Nahn is a Professor of physics at M.I.T.

161
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:16,030
Nahn和几千个科学家一道 用LHC把原子轰成碎片
Using the LHC,Nahn and thousands of other scientists

162
00:09:16,030 --> 00:09:19,670
使之进行时间旅行
turn pieces of atoms into time travelers.

163
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:21,340
他们把质子加速
They take protons,

164
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:24,680
直到接近光速
accelerate them to nearly the speed of light,

165
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,510
让它们撞到一起
then smash them together.

166
00:09:26,510 --> 00:09:30,480
碰撞产生亚原子粒子
The subatomic particles that come out of the explosions

167
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:33,680
这些粒子是短命鬼 存活约十亿分之一秒
only live for about a billionth of a second.

168
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:37,150
但在LHC里，十亿分之一秒
But in the LHC,that billionth of a second

169
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,800
被拉伸了
is stretched out relative to our time.

170
00:09:39,690 --> 00:09:41,860
欧洲粒子物理研究所（CERN）的LHC 像是一个时间机器
The LHC here at CERN is like a time machine

171
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,830
具备有趣的物理特征
because of a funny feature of physics.

172
00:09:43,830 --> 00:09:45,760
速度和你认为的不一样
Velocity is not what you think it is.

173
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:48,570
普通级别的速度没啥了不起
Velocity at normal speeds is normal,

174
00:09:48,570 --> 00:09:52,800
但在非常非常高速的情况下 速度有一个上限
but at very,very high speeds,velocity has a maximum limit.

175
00:09:52,810 --> 00:09:54,310
因此在对撞机里的质子
So the protons in the ring

176
00:09:54,310 --> 00:09:56,540
只能以接近光速的速度飞行
are traveling near the speed of light,

177
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:59,780
却不能变得更快
and they can't go faster.

178
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:00,980
于此同时
What happens instead

179
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:03,350
它们的时间开始变慢
is that their clocks start moving slower.

180
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:05,580
它们的”滴答“比我们的”滴答“ 间隔更长
Their ticks are longer than our ticks.

181
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:08,790
某种意义上，对撞机里 飞行的质子
So in some sense,the protons that are going around the ring,

182
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:11,360
它们的时钟比我们的慢
their clocks are moving slower than our clocks,

183
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,890
和我们比起来，它们像是时间旅行者
so they're like time travelers relative to us.

184
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:19,900
弗里曼:CERN里 进行时间旅行的质子告诉我们
Freeman:The time-travelling protons at CERN

185
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:24,440
我们也可以在时间里遨游
show us that we,too,can travel far forward in time.

186
00:10:27,270 --> 00:10:28,540
几十年后
Decades from now,

187
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:31,640
接近光速的太空船
spaceships traveling near the speed of light

188
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,810
也许要执行10年的任务
could fly into the stars on a 10-year mission.

189
00:10:34,810 --> 00:10:37,650
对船上的人来说，那是10年
For the people onboard,it would be 10 years.

190
00:10:37,650 --> 00:10:41,720
而地球上，那是1000年
On earth,a thousand years would pass.

191
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:46,990
回程的宇航员将到达一个 完全不同的未来世界
The astronauts would return to a far different future world.

192
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:50,560
飞向未来的时间旅行是可能的
Time travel into the future is possible.

193
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:54,100
但这会是一个单程旅行吗？
But is it a one-way trip?

194
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,000
我们往返过去未来的
Can we make our dream

195
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,300
时间旅行之梦会成真吗?
of time travel backwards and forwards come true?

196
00:11:08,450 --> 00:11:09,950
用科技手段
With the right technology,

197
00:11:09,950 --> 00:11:13,160
我们可以到达未来
time-traveling spaceships could take us into the future.

198
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:19,600
但我们能逆流而上，回到过去吗？
But can we go against the era of time and journey into the past?

199
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:22,970
呃，这可能不像听上去那么难
Well,it might not b be as hard as it sounds.

200
00:11:22,970 --> 00:11:26,370
我的意思是，毕竟，过去就在我们身边
I mean,after all,the past is all around us.

201
00:11:26,370 --> 00:11:28,370
想想这个
Consider this.

202
00:11:28,370 --> 00:11:34,210
光速是每秒钟30万千米
The speed of light is 186,000 miles per second.

203
00:11:34,210 --> 00:11:36,380
为什么，那已经快的变态了
Why,that's awfully fast.

204
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:40,820
但是当一束光从这里 飞向那里
But when a piece of light travels from here to there,

205
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,190
还是需要时间的
it takes time.

206
00:11:42,190 --> 00:11:45,720
那意味着，你目之所及
And that means that everywhere you look,

207
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,960
实际上都是过去的事情
you're looking back in time.

208
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:51,860
光传播一英尺
It takes one billionth of a second

209
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:54,700
需要十亿分之一秒
for light to travel one foot.

210
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:58,130
所以你看到的旁边的家伙
So you see the person you're sitting next to

211
00:11:58,140 --> 00:12:01,540
是十亿分之一秒前的历史人
a billionth of a second in the past.

212
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:05,980
我们看到的太阳光是8分钟之前的
The light from the sun is eight minutes old when we see it.

213
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:08,880
当我们观察星空
And the deeper we gaze into the sky,

214
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:11,680
距离越远，我们看到的越古老
the farther we see back in time.

215
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:16,020
卫星给宇宙边缘拍了照
Satellites have photographed the edge of the universe,

216
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:19,960
137亿光年之外
13.7 billion light-years away.

217
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:26,630
照片拍的是137亿年前的景象
That's 13.7 billion years back in time.

218
00:12:26,630 --> 00:12:29,130
我们一直在观察过去
We always look into the past.

219
00:12:29,130 --> 00:12:32,270
但是，还有更精彩的
But it goes even deeper than that.

220
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:36,370
根据爱因斯坦的理论 时间和空间相像
According to Einstein,time is just like space.

221
00:12:36,370 --> 00:12:39,680
由于每一寸空间都存在于此
Since every bit of space exists here right now,

222
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:42,150
这意味着，每一寸时间
that means that every bit of time

223
00:12:42,150 --> 00:12:44,580
也存在于此
exists right here right now,too.

224
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,960
Sean Carroll是一个物理学家
Sean Carroll is a physicist

225
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:55,390
供职于加州理工学院
at the California institute of Technology.

226
00:12:55,390 --> 00:12:58,900
Carroll:物理学家一般都信奉永恒主义
Carroll:Physicists tend to be eternalists.

227
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,760
他们认为我们所处的整个宇宙
They think that the whole universe,

228
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:03,430
整个的四维时空
the whole four-dimensional space-time in which we live,

229
00:13:03,430 --> 00:13:04,900
是真实的
is equally real.

230
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:09,170
我们存在于这个时空连续统一体 的不同时刻
We exist at different moments in this space-time continuum,

231
00:13:09,170 --> 00:13:12,440
我们会在不同的时刻 感受不同的事情
and we feel different things at different moments of time.

232
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:15,950
但这不是说随着时间流逝 未来正变为真实
But it's not that the future is becoming real as time goes on.

233
00:13:15,950 --> 00:13:17,750
未来是存在的
It's just that the future exists

234
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:20,220
就像过去和现在这样存在
just as much as the past or the present.

235
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:23,720
我们只不过随着时间的步调 发现未来发生了什么
We're discovering what happens in the future as time goes on.

236
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:26,120
未来成真和过去成真
But it's not becoming any more real

237
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:28,090
是差不多的
than the past is becoming real.

238
00:13:28,090 --> 00:13:29,530
我们考虑这样的原理
So we think that,in principle,

239
00:13:29,530 --> 00:13:32,060
过去和未来如同现实一样存在
the past and the future exist just as much as the present.

240
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,800
弗里曼:我们被整个时间所环绕
Freeman:The whole of time is all around us.

241
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:43,170
但我们能够从当前跳回过去吗？
But can we jump from the present to the past?

242
00:13:44,510 --> 00:13:47,580
在20世纪早期
In the early years of the 20th century,

243
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:50,450
一个叫做阿尔伯特 爱因斯坦的 年轻专利局职员
a young patent clerk named Albert Einstein

244
00:13:50,450 --> 00:13:52,280
给我们一个可能回到过去的办法
gave us a possible way back.

245
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:54,480
坐在去上班的有轨电车上
Riding to work on a streetcar,

246
00:13:54,490 --> 00:13:58,790
20出头的爱因斯坦 仰头看着一个钟楼
the barely 20-year-old Einstein looked up at a clock tower,

247
00:13:58,790 --> 00:14:01,160
突然，钟楼报时
and suddenly it all clicked.

248
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:10,570
爱因斯坦意识到时间 和你所处位置有关
Einstein realized that time is relative to where you are

249
00:14:10,570 --> 00:14:13,200
还和你的运动速度有关
and how fast you're moving.

250
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,810
时间是第四维
Time is the fourth dimension,

251
00:14:15,810 --> 00:14:20,740
与空间之维——长宽高
bound tightly together with length,width,and depth --

252
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:23,250
紧密联系
the dimensions of space.

253
00:14:23,250 --> 00:14:26,550
几年后，爱因斯坦用他的
A few years later,Einstein used his ideas

254
00:14:26,550 --> 00:14:29,750
引力场对时空的作用这一理论
about gravity's effect on space and time

255
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:33,120
创造了描绘宇宙的数学地图
to create a mathematical map of the cosmos.

256
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:40,030
他证明，时间和空间 的构造是扭曲的
He proved that the fabric of space and time is curved.

257
00:14:40,030 --> 00:14:42,300
如果宇宙是扭曲的
If the universe is curved,

258
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:46,340
那就有可能建造一座桥跨越它
there might be ways to build bridges across it

259
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:48,840
或在其内部建立环路
or create loops inside of it,

260
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:52,810
这些环路给时间旅行带来可能
loops that will allow time travel.

261
00:14:52,810 --> 00:14:56,050
这一切由数学天才Kurt Godel
That was the conclusion reached in 1949

262
00:14:56,050 --> 00:14:59,820
于1949年证明
by the mathematical genius Kurt Godel.

263
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:02,490
Godel 是爱因斯坦的好友
Godel was a close friend of Einstein's,

264
00:15:02,490 --> 00:15:03,950
他打算看看
and he decided to see

265
00:15:03,950 --> 00:15:07,290
这个伟人的理论 是否允许时间旅行
if the great man's equations permitted time travel.

266
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:09,390
他发现答案是肯定的
He found that they did.

267
00:15:09,390 --> 00:15:12,800
如果在宇宙围绕坐标轴旋转时
If the universe rotates on its axis

268
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:16,570
你能设法保持不动
and you somehow remain perfectly still,

269
00:15:16,570 --> 00:15:18,270
那么你就有可能
it would be possible

270
00:15:18,270 --> 00:15:22,140
到宇宙中的任何时间和地点
to go to any time and place in the universe --

271
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:24,610
这是激动人心的发现，只是
an exciting discovery,

272
00:15:24,610 --> 00:15:30,610
我们知道宇宙并不旋转
except that we now know that the universe does not rotate.

273
00:15:30,610 --> 00:15:34,780
没有旋转，就没有时间旅行
And without the rotation,you cannot have time travel.

274
00:15:34,790 --> 00:15:39,160
Godel的解答是不现实的
Godel's solution was unrealistic,

275
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,720
但他的激进思想
but his radical thinking

276
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:43,330
激励了新一代的探索者
inspired a new generation of explorers.

277
00:15:43,330 --> 00:15:48,230
Frank Tipler教授是追寻Godel足迹
Professor Frank Tipler was one of the renegade physicists

278
00:15:48,230 --> 00:15:51,400
前卫的物理学者之一
who followed in Godel's footsteps.

279
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:54,270
我还没从麻省理工毕业的时候
I was fascinated by Godel's paper,

280
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:58,910
就被Godel的论文迷住了
which I had actually read when I was an undergraduate at MIT,

281
00:15:58,910 --> 00:16:02,850
我想试试，看能不能 证明爱因斯坦的假设
and I wondered if I could follow up Einstein's suggestion,

282
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:05,550
这一切在物理学上是可能的吗？
can this be actually done physically?

283
00:16:05,550 --> 00:16:09,820
我们不能旋转宇宙—
We can't rotate the universe -- it either is rotating or not --

284
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:13,920
可我么也许能在小点的尺度上 做些尝试
but we might be able to do something on a smaller scale.

285
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:17,560
现实中，一个明显的，容易解决的模型是
An obvious,easy-to-solve model in relativity

286
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,500
一个旋转的圆柱体
was a rotating cylinder.

287
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:23,330
我能展示，一个旋转的圆柱体
And so I was able to show that a rotating cylinder

288
00:16:23,330 --> 00:16:26,440
会导致时间的回路
would give rise to these loops in time,

289
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:29,370
使得回到过去成为可能
being able to go backwards into time.

290
00:16:29,370 --> 00:16:33,380
弗里曼:Tipler的巨大圆柱 也许悬在宇宙空间里
Freeman:Tipler's gigantic cylinder would hang in space,

291
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:36,280
以光速旋转
whirling at nearly the speed of light.

292
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:40,450
当时空在圆柱周围缠绕
Space turns into time and time into space

293
00:16:40,450 --> 00:16:43,490
空间转换为时间 时间转换为空间
as both become twisted around the cylinder.

294
00:16:43,490 --> 00:16:46,560
当向这个圆柱靠近
So by traveling forward around the cylinder,

295
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:50,690
你就回到过去
you go backwards in time.

296
00:16:50,690 --> 00:16:52,830
时间的方向是这边
Time direction is this way,

297
00:16:52,830 --> 00:16:56,070
但当环绕着一个 非常快的物体时
but around a very rapidly rotating body,

298
00:16:56,070 --> 00:16:59,600
你能在这样一个螺旋 里向回运动
you can go backwards into a spiral like this

299
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,840
回到过去
and go backwards into time.

300
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:08,180
我的名为“制作时间机器”的论文
So my paper,which I tried to get published

301
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:11,880
正在准备印刷发行
under the title of "constructing a time machine,"

302
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:15,650
编辑同志认为这题目太不河蟹了
the editors thought that was a little too radical,

303
00:17:15,650 --> 00:17:21,220
他们想要个不那么刺激的名字
and they wanted something that would not be so sound-bitey,

304
00:17:21,230 --> 00:17:25,960
于是我给论文改了名，叫做
and so I changed the title to "rotating cylinders

305
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:30,570
“旋转的圆柱以及 全局因果性的违反”
and the possibility of global causality violation."

306
00:17:30,570 --> 00:17:34,540
额滴神啊，一个长到不知所云的标题 如果不读正文
Now,there is a mouthful that no one will catch on to

307
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:37,370
你就不知道这个论文是讲什么的 （译者：这就是不给编辑送钱的下场）
unless you actually read the paper.

308
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:41,810
弗里曼:但是后来，Tipler发现
Freeman:But later,Tipler found

309
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,610
他的想法中有几个问题
there are a few problems with his idea.

310
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:47,820
Tipler:我意识到这个旋转的圆柱
Tipler:I realized that the rotating cylinder,

311
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:50,990
虽然是爱因斯坦方程的一个
although an easy-to-construct solution

312
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:52,520
较为容易的解决办法
to the Einstein equations,

313
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:53,860
但还是不太现实
was not very realistic

314
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:56,390
因为圆柱必须是 无限的
because it had to be an infinite cylinder,

315
00:17:56,390 --> 00:17:58,490
而创造一个无限的圆柱
and creating an infinite cylinder

316
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:00,630
难度堪比创造宇宙
is as hard as creating a universe,

317
00:18:00,630 --> 00:18:02,600
很明显，我们法力不够
which,obviously,we cannot do.

318
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:05,370
于是我试图寻找，看看是不是可能
So I was wondering if it would be possible

319
00:18:05,370 --> 00:18:09,210
在一个小得多的尺度上 创建此类的结果
to have this sort of structure in a much smaller scale,

320
00:18:09,210 --> 00:18:13,010
我发现了，额滴神啊，这是根本不可能的
and I discovered,alas,that's not going to be possible.

321
00:18:13,010 --> 00:18:14,440
因为当你试图
Because if you tried

322
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:17,780
加速一个物体 创建时间机器
to speed up a body to generate the time machine,

323
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:19,180
你会发现
what you would find

324
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:22,320
在时间机器成型之前
before the time-machine property was created,

325
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:26,590
你会在时空上扯出个口子
you would rip a hole in space and time.

326
00:18:26,590 --> 00:18:32,830
你会在时间和空间中 创造一个奇点
You would create a singularity right there in space and time.

327
00:18:32,830 --> 00:18:35,130
所以，-_-|| 我的梦想破灭了
So,alas,I had to give up my dream

328
00:18:35,130 --> 00:18:36,770
时间机器是水中月，镜中花 发改委说要降油价——没戏
of creating a time machine.

329
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:41,870
弗里曼:Tipler的旋转圆柱无法工作
Freeman:Tipler's spinning cylinder might not work,

330
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:44,710
但在宇宙中存在大量的物体
but there are massive objects in the universe

331
00:18:44,710 --> 00:18:47,910
它们以接近光速的速度旋转—
that are already spinning near the speed of light --

332
00:18:47,910 --> 00:18:50,850
黑洞
black holes.

333
00:18:50,850 --> 00:18:53,050
黑洞的巨大质量
The immense gravity of black holes

334
00:18:53,050 --> 00:18:56,790
将物理定律推向极致
push the laws of physics to the extremes.

335
00:18:56,790 --> 00:19:00,160
时间回溯的秘密 会藏身于黑洞的
Could the secrets of backwards time travel

336
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:02,360
阴森深处吗？
lurk in their Stygian depths?

337
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:09,270
黑洞是体积很小 但密度极高的物体
Black holes are small but incredibly massive objects

338
00:19:09,390 --> 00:19:12,420
散布在宇宙之中
scattered throughout the universe.

339
00:19:12,430 --> 00:19:14,960
黑洞的极端引力
The intense gravity of a black hole

340
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:17,460
比任何已知的天体
warps the fabric of time and space

341
00:19:17,460 --> 00:19:22,270
更加严重的扭曲时空结构
more than any other celestial object we know of.

342
00:19:22,270 --> 00:19:26,240
黑洞扭曲事件的能力 可以被驾驭吗？
Can the time-warping properties of black holes be harnessed?

343
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:29,810
我们能利用它 穿越时间吗？
Can we use them to travel through time?

344
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,720
黑洞并不是时间机器
Black holes are not time machines.

345
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:39,050
你会落入奇点
You would fall into a singularity,

346
00:19:39,050 --> 00:19:41,690
你会被撕裂，去拜见马克思
and you'd be crushed,and you would die.

347
00:19:41,690 --> 00:19:44,590
我们还不完全了解 黑洞中心都发生
Some interesting effect that we don't yet understand

348
00:19:44,590 --> 00:19:47,330
什么有趣的事件
about what happens at the center of a black hole,

349
00:19:47,330 --> 00:19:48,490
没有理由相信
there's no reason to think

350
00:19:48,490 --> 00:19:50,230
黑洞会把你带回过去
that it pushes you backward in time.

351
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:53,060
黑洞多少有点像 “躲猫猫”的看守所
The black hole is more or less a one-way street.

352
00:19:53,070 --> 00:19:55,700
你进去了 就甭想再出来了
You go in. You will never come back out.

353
00:19:59,170 --> 00:20:01,370
弗里曼:所以黑洞是不行滴
Freeman:So black holes won't work.

354
00:20:01,370 --> 00:20:04,680
但是另一个凭借科幻小说出名 的宇宙异常现象
But another cosmic anomaly made famous by science fiction

355
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:06,580
也许派得上用场—
might do the trick --

356
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:09,480
虫洞
wormholes.

357
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:13,850
虫洞是连接两个 遥远地点的魔法门
Wormholes are magic doorways connecting two remote locations.

358
00:20:13,850 --> 00:20:15,650
这些宇宙天桥
These cosmic sky bridges

359
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:20,390
能让我们在空间中跳跃 在时间中旅行
would allow us to jump across space and travel in time.

360
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:23,560
飞进一个虫洞
Fly into a wormhole,

361
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:27,400
你能找到通向 其他时间或空间的捷径
and you can take a shortcut to another place or time.

362
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:30,670
我们没有虫洞存在的证据
We have no proof that wormholes exist,

363
00:20:30,670 --> 00:20:34,710
但有大量坚实可靠的 科学支持这一观点
but there is plenty of solid science behind them.

364
00:20:34,710 --> 00:20:37,610
没有人比著名的 物理学家Kip Thorne
No one knows more about wormholes

365
00:20:37,610 --> 00:20:40,780
更了解虫洞了.
than renowned physicist Kip Thorne.

366
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:45,720
他能告诉你们这些菜鸟 虫洞因何得名
For starters,he can tell you why they're called wormholes.

367
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:50,820
如果你有一个苹果，一个虫子蛀穿了它
If you have an apple,a worm drills a hole through the apple,

368
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:52,590
从一面到了另一面
reaches from one side to the other,

369
00:20:52,590 --> 00:20:54,530
你可以把苹果表面
you can think of the surface of the apple

370
00:20:54,530 --> 00:20:55,860
想像成我们的宇宙
as being like our universe,

371
00:20:55,860 --> 00:21:00,230
虫子穿过了高维空间
and the worm has gone through some higher dimension

372
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:02,300
到了另一边
to reach the other side.

373
00:21:04,340 --> 00:21:09,640
弗里曼:如果虫洞存在，它们要比原子还小
Freeman:If they exist,wormholes are smaller than atoms.

374
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:12,640
如果我们想穿过去
If we want to go through them,

375
00:21:12,650 --> 00:21:16,010
我们需要扩大它们，并保持它们开放
we need to stretch them out and hold them open.

376
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:17,380
打开一个虫洞
Prying open a wormhole

377
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:20,050
也许要极其巨大的能量—
would take a tremendous amount of energy --

378
00:21:20,050 --> 00:21:22,550
还不只是常规能量
not just ordinary energy,

379
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:26,360
而是称作反能量的东东
but something called negative energy.

380
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:30,060
反能量是反引力的
Negative energy is antigravitational.

381
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:33,830
它排斥时空结构
It repels the fabric of space and time

382
00:21:33,830 --> 00:21:39,400
阻止引力消灭虫洞
and would prevent gravity from crushing a wormhole.

383
00:21:39,410 --> 00:21:40,870
问题是—
One problem --

384
00:21:40,870 --> 00:21:45,710
很多人不相信反能量的存在
a lot of people don't believe negative energy exists.

385
00:21:45,710 --> 00:21:49,950
反引力的能量是荒唐可笑的
The kind of energy that would antigravitate is ridiculous.

386
00:21:49,950 --> 00:21:52,280
但实际上，在现代物理学中
But in fact,in modern physics,

387
00:21:52,290 --> 00:21:55,190
我们有反能量的例子
we know examples of negative energy

388
00:21:55,190 --> 00:21:58,860
在实验室里天天 被创造出来
that are created in the laboratory every day --

389
00:21:58,860 --> 00:22:02,760
很小剂量的反能量 经常转瞬即逝
small l amounts of negative energy,often just transient,

390
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:05,360
但是尽管如此 仍然存在反能量
but nevertheless,negative energy.

391
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:08,100
所以我不愿意
And so I was not willing

392
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:10,270
排除这种可能性
to dismiss this possibility out of hand.

393
00:22:10,270 --> 00:22:11,600
关键问题是
The fundamental question

394
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:15,010
一个先进文明有可能
was could a very advanced civilization

395
00:22:15,010 --> 00:22:18,080
积累足够的反能量
accumulate enough negative energy

396
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:21,850
并在虫洞内部保存它
and hold it in the interior of the wormhole

397
00:22:21,850 --> 00:22:25,180
来支撑虫洞的存在
long enough to keep the wormhole open

398
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:28,820
以使某人穿越虫洞
so that somebody could travel through it.

399
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:31,390
答案是，我们不知道
The answer is we don't know.

400
00:22:34,430 --> 00:22:38,630
弗里曼:同时，另一个物理学叛徒
Freeman:Meanwhile,another renegade physicist

401
00:22:38,630 --> 00:22:41,270
找到了不同的驾驭方法
worked up a different way to harness

402
00:22:41,270 --> 00:22:44,640
来控制造成时间撕裂效应 的天体现象
the time-warping effects of celestial phenomena.

403
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:48,440
Richard Gott研究时间旅行的历史
Richard Gott has been studying the problem of time travel

404
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,940
有几十年了
for decades.

405
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:51,880
Gott的新型时间机器
Gott's novel time machine

406
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:55,580
利用环绕宇宙弦的 强大重力
uses the heavy gravity surrounding cosmic strings

407
00:22:55,580 --> 00:22:58,780
创造时间回路
to create loops in time.

408
00:22:58,780 --> 00:23:03,190
宇宙弦是能量细线
Cosmic strings are thin strands of energy

409
00:23:03,190 --> 00:23:05,960
也许横穿宇宙
that may run through the universe.

410
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,090
有这么首诗
There's a poem.

411
00:23:07,090 --> 00:23:09,230
“年轻小妇人，名叫晶晶亮
"There was a young lady named 'bright.'

412
00:23:09,230 --> 00:23:11,400
跑的非常快，光也难追上
"she traveled far faster than light.

413
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,530
今日离家去，踏上相对路
"She left one day in a relative way,

414
00:23:13,530 --> 00:23:15,800
回到家中时，在昨天晚上”
and returned home the previous night."

415
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:18,270
麻烦的是，爱因斯坦也告诉你
The trouble is,Einstein also told you

416
00:23:18,270 --> 00:23:20,510
你不可能建造一艘
that you can't build a spaceship

417
00:23:20,510 --> 00:23:23,170
速度超过光速的飞船
that goes faster than the speed of light.

418
00:23:23,180 --> 00:23:25,880
但在关于时空扭曲的
But in general relativity,

419
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:28,410
广义相对论里
which is theory of curved space-time,

420
00:23:28,410 --> 00:23:31,620
如果你能走捷径 就能快过光速
if you take a shortcut,you can beat a light.

421
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:35,420
因此，这就允许你环绕宇宙弦
So this is what allows you to circle the cosmic strings

422
00:23:35,420 --> 00:23:39,220
像晶晶亮小姐一样 回到过去
and,like miss Bright,visit an event in your own past.

423
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:46,000
弗里曼:没人知道宇宙弦是否真存在
Freeman:And no one knows if cosmic strings are real.

424
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:49,200
可是许多物理学家 认为它们就在那里—
But many physicists think they're out there --

425
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:51,840
那些高密度真空能量碎片
pieces of high-density vacuum energy

426
00:23:51,840 --> 00:23:53,810
宇宙大爆炸的残留物
left over from the big bang,

427
00:23:53,810 --> 00:23:58,340
比原子核还袖珍
narrower than an atomic nucleus.

428
00:23:58,340 --> 00:24:02,550
某些弦可能很短 某些则无限长
Some strings may be short. Some may be infinitely long.

429
00:24:02,550 --> 00:24:05,650
但它们都产生极大引力
But they all exert incredible gravity.

430
00:24:05,650 --> 00:24:08,650
在有极大引力的地方
And where there's incredible gravity,

431
00:24:08,650 --> 00:24:13,290
就有可能产生穿越时空的捷径
there's a chance of creating a shortcut across time and space.

432
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:20,030
这就是利用宇宙弦 创建时间机器的方法
So here's how to build a time machine using cosmic strings.

433
00:24:20,030 --> 00:24:21,470
现在，你也许会想
Now,you might think

434
00:24:21,470 --> 00:24:24,270
围绕宇宙弦的几何结构
that the geometry around a cosmic string

435
00:24:24,270 --> 00:24:26,300
会像个批萨饼那样平
is flat like a piece of pizza.

436
00:24:26,310 --> 00:24:28,370
实际上，因为每单位长度的弦
But actually,because they have

437
00:24:28,370 --> 00:24:31,340
都有巨大的质量
a large mass per unit length in the string,

438
00:24:31,340 --> 00:24:34,410
形状更像是少了一块的批萨饼
it really looks like a pizza with a slice missing.

439
00:24:34,410 --> 00:24:39,680
如果我切掉一块批萨 拿到一边
So if I cut out a slice of pizza here,take it away,

440
00:24:39,690 --> 00:24:43,320
当我折起批萨时 它就像个漏斗
and then I fold up the pizza so it's like a cone,

441
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:46,690
批萨看上去像— 它像个漏斗
it looks like -- the pizza looks like a cone.

442
00:24:46,690 --> 00:24:49,290
如果我在这儿 星球A
So if I was over here on planet "A,"

443
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:52,860
我能向星球B发一束光
I can send a light beam to planet "B."

444
00:24:52,870 --> 00:24:55,170
我可以登上一艘宇宙飞船
But I could get on a spaceship,

445
00:24:55,170 --> 00:24:57,840
我可以以比光慢的飞行速度
and I could go slower than the speed of light

446
00:24:57,840 --> 00:25:00,370
从这个地方，穿过捷径
and travel over here across this shortcut,

447
00:25:00,370 --> 00:25:03,010
到达这里，赶在光线头里到达
and I can get there ahead of the light beam.

448
00:25:03,010 --> 00:25:06,540
这意味着，我的出发地和到达地
And what that means is that my departure and my arrival

449
00:25:06,550 --> 00:25:11,220
在空间中的距离 比时间中的距离更远
are separated by more distance in space than distance in time.

450
00:25:11,220 --> 00:25:14,990
换句话说，这可能是4光年的距离
In other words,this might be four light-years in distance

451
00:25:14,990 --> 00:25:16,890
时间上却只是3年的时间差
and only three years in time.

452
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:19,260
这样，你能像我这样
So then what you could do

453
00:25:19,260 --> 00:25:24,030
在这里切掉另一块批萨
is I could cut out another missing pizza slice here,

454
00:25:24,030 --> 00:25:26,600
我就有了两条宇宙弦
and now I've got two cosmic strings.

455
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:30,170
折起来，像个船
And then fold it up like a boat.

456
00:25:30,170 --> 00:25:31,600
这就是两条宇宙弦周围的
That's what space-time

457
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:34,310
时空的样子
around the two cosmic strings looks like.

458
00:25:34,310 --> 00:25:36,170
这样，如果我的宇宙飞船
So then what I can do

459
00:25:36,180 --> 00:25:39,710
环绕这两根宇宙弦
is if I circle the two cosmic strings with my spaceship,

460
00:25:38,180 --> 00:25:39,710
我就能够

461
00:25:39,710 --> 00:25:43,210
在正午抵达星球A
I can arrive back to planet "A" at noon.

462
00:25:43,220 --> 00:25:47,490
现在，正午的星球A 是同一时间的同一地点
Now,planet "A" at noon is the same time and the same place.

463
00:25:47,490 --> 00:25:51,820
于是我可以回来，和出发时的我 握握手
So I can come back and shake hands with myself as I departed.

464
00:25:51,820 --> 00:25:55,930
那个老点的我可以回来，我可以看到我自己出发
So my older self can come back,and I can see myself off.

465
00:25:55,930 --> 00:25:59,930
我回到过去，和自己交流
This is me visiting an event in my own past.

466
00:25:59,930 --> 00:26:03,200
这是真正的回到过去的旅行
That's real time travel to the past.

467
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:10,680
弗里曼:但是，再一次，有一两个问题
Freeman:But,once again,there are one or two problems with this.

468
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:12,010
对于新手
For starters,

469
00:26:12,010 --> 00:26:15,610
当你把两个宇宙弦高速靠近
when you push two cosmic strings together at high speed,

470
00:26:15,610 --> 00:26:18,520
可能创造出黑洞
it may create a black hole.

471
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:23,560
Gott:时间旅行后，你可能小命不保
Gott:You may be killed after doing the time travel,

472
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:24,820
也有可能在完成旅行前
or you could be killed

473
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:27,230
就被干掉了
before you even complete the time travel.

474
00:26:27,230 --> 00:26:29,860
另一个问题是，如果你想在一年内返回
The other thing is that this loop

475
00:26:29,860 --> 00:26:33,600
这个回路的质量 也许会达到
would weigh about maybe half the mass of our galaxy

476
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:36,900
我们星系的一半之多
if you wanted to travel back in time a year.

477
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:38,770
所以，这个工程
And so this is a project

478
00:26:38,770 --> 00:26:42,170
只有超文明才能尝试
that only supercivilizations could attempt.

479
00:26:42,170 --> 00:26:45,180
这远远超出了我们的能力
It's far beyond what we're able to do.

480
00:26:46,910 --> 00:26:48,450
弗里曼:Gott这样的物理学家
Freeman:Physicists like Gott

481
00:26:48,450 --> 00:26:51,950
还没有声称能够建造 可用的时间机器
don't claim they can build working time machines today.

482
00:26:51,950 --> 00:26:54,420
他们只是在试图证明
They're trying to figure out

483
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:59,120
物理定律是否允许时间旅行
whether the laws of physics permit time travel at all.

484
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:02,960
所有建造 时间机器的方案
There are several inherent problems in all scenarios

485
00:27:02,960 --> 00:27:05,000
都存在固有的问题
for building time machines.

486
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:11,370
自然似乎在宣示 在你试图激活时间机器时
And that is that nature appears to have a driving force

487
00:27:11,370 --> 00:27:15,170
总会有这样那样的原因
that may always cause a time machine to self-destruct

488
00:27:15,170 --> 00:27:18,010
导致机器的自我破坏
at the moment you try to activate it.

489
00:27:20,910 --> 00:27:24,780
能否绕过这些陷阱？我们相信
The answer as to whether you can get around it

490
00:27:24,780 --> 00:27:27,620
问题的答案
is held tightly in the grips,we believe,

491
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:30,020
就存在于量子力学的定律
of the laws of quantum gravity --

492
00:27:30,020 --> 00:27:32,420
那些我们还不了解的定律
laws that we don't yet understand.

493
00:27:34,430 --> 00:27:38,860
弗里曼:我们知道引力如何影响宏观物理，譬如人，
Freeman:We know how gravity affects large objects like people,

494
00:27:38,860 --> 00:27:41,570
我们的星球和空中其他星星
our planet,and the stars in the sky.

495
00:27:41,570 --> 00:27:44,000
我们并不了解，在量子级别
We don't understand how it works

496
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,470
在波和粒子的极小范围
deep down at the quantum level --

497
00:27:46,470 --> 00:27:50,780
引力如何作用
the supersmall domain of waves and particles.

498
00:27:50,780 --> 00:27:53,080
但是对某物的不了解
But not understanding something

499
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:55,550
从未阻止人们开展试验
has never stopped people from experimenting.

500
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:59,640
看上去，在爱因斯坦的时空世界里
It seems that time travel is next to impossible

501
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:02,880
时间旅行几乎是不可能的
in Einstein's world of space and time.

502
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:07,580
但有另一个世界，和另一类物理学
But there's another world and another kind of physics

503
00:28:07,580 --> 00:28:12,420
在那里，爱因斯坦的理论不再成立
where Einstein's rational rules don't always apply.

504
00:28:12,420 --> 00:28:16,020
那就是原子深处的世界
It's the world deep inside the atom,

505
00:28:16,020 --> 00:28:21,100
古怪的量子力学当家作主的地方
where the weird laws of quantum mechanics take hold.

506
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:23,360
现在，表被吓倒啊
Now,don't be scared.

507
00:28:23,370 --> 00:28:27,570
奇怪但却迷人
This is strange but fascinating stuff.

508
00:28:32,510 --> 00:28:34,640
量子力学认为
Quantum mechanics is just the idea

509
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:37,950
实际存在要比我们所观察到的 丰富的多
that what exists is much richer than what you can observe.

510
00:28:37,950 --> 00:28:41,150
当你看粒子时，你看到它在一个地方
So when you look at a particle,you see it in one place.

511
00:28:41,150 --> 00:28:43,220
量子力学认为，当你不看它时
Quantum mechanics says that when you're not looking at it,

512
00:28:43,220 --> 00:28:45,420
这个粒子遍布空间各处
that particle exists all over the place.

513
00:28:45,420 --> 00:28:46,620
这就像是
Maybe it's more likely

514
00:28:46,620 --> 00:28:48,790
你会在这里或那里 看到它
that you'll see it one place or another,

515
00:28:48,790 --> 00:28:51,260
但实际上，有一个可能性的分布
but there's really a spectrum of possibilities

516
00:28:51,260 --> 00:28:54,730
决定了你会在哪里 观察到这个粒子
for where you will see the particle.

517
00:28:54,730 --> 00:28:57,400
当你把量子力学的理论
So when you combine the ideas of quantum mechanics

518
00:28:57,400 --> 00:29:00,200
和时间旅行的想法结合时，热闹的大戏开场了
with the ideas of time travel,all hell breaks loose.

519
00:29:03,940 --> 00:29:07,980
弗里曼:量子力学的最奇怪 特点之一
Freeman:One of the strangest properties of quantum mechanics

520
00:29:07,980 --> 00:29:11,080
称作“非定域性”
is called "nonlocality."

521
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:15,880
两个粒子彼此存在感应
It's when two particles instantly affect each other,

522
00:29:15,880 --> 00:29:20,120
即使它们相隔数英里 甚至一光年之远
even when they're miles or light-years apart.

523
00:29:20,120 --> 00:29:23,790
相当像是巫毒巫术
It's a bit like voodoo.

524
00:29:23,790 --> 00:29:28,860
当你刺人偶，人就马上感到疼痛
When you stab the doll,the human being is also affected.

525
00:29:28,860 --> 00:29:30,800
可与巫毒巫术不同的是
But unlike voodoo,

526
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:34,940
量子非定域性根正苗红 是经过科学证明的
quantum nonlocality is scientifically proven.

527
00:29:37,810 --> 00:29:41,910
今天，瑞士银行基金资助相关研究
Today,Swiss banks fund experiments

528
00:29:41,910 --> 00:29:44,250
看看非定域性能否用于开发
to see if nonlocality can be used

529
00:29:44,250 --> 00:29:47,450
某种无法破解的
to make one-of-a-kind,crack-proof security keys

530
00:29:47,450 --> 00:29:50,220
电子转账密钥
for computer transactions.

531
00:29:50,220 --> 00:29:55,060
Nicolas Gisin教授领导这项研究
Professor Nicolas Gisin leads the way.

532
00:29:55,060 --> 00:29:57,960
量子物理和光纤专家Gisin
A quantum physicist and fiber-optic specialist,

533
00:29:57,960 --> 00:30:01,060
他测试了量子非定域性
Gisin has tested quantum nonlocality

534
00:30:01,060 --> 00:30:04,700
距离遥远的光子之间
by showing the perfect synchronization of photons,

535
00:30:04,700 --> 00:30:09,300
具有完美的同步性
particles of light,separated by great distances.

536
00:30:09,300 --> 00:30:12,240
量子物理说，呃 实际情况是
Quantum physics says,well,what happens

537
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:15,680
当你对一个光子施加影响
is that whenever you do something on one photon,

538
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:18,610
有反应的并不只是这个光子
the reaction is not on this photon only,

539
00:30:18,610 --> 00:30:21,550
这两个光子会产生一个整体反应
but there's a global reaction of two photons.

540
00:30:21,550 --> 00:30:23,720
这意味着，这两个光子
In some sense,the two photons,

541
00:30:23,720 --> 00:30:26,720
虽然远隔千山万水
although they are at this large distance,

542
00:30:26,720 --> 00:30:29,220
它们仍然构成了一个系统
they still constitute one system.

543
00:30:29,220 --> 00:30:32,990
这个整体的系统会立即反应
And so the global system reacts at once.

544
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,860
这就是量子非定域性
And this is quantum nonlocality.

545
00:30:35,860 --> 00:30:39,330
弗里曼:Gisin通过横穿日内瓦的光纤
Freeman:Gisin sends photon signals

546
00:30:39,330 --> 00:30:42,670
发送光子信号
through fiber-optic cables stretched across Geneva.

547
00:30:42,670 --> 00:30:47,610
一端的一对光子被激光激活
A pair of photons on one end is activated with a laser.

548
00:30:47,610 --> 00:30:52,080
另一端的光子马上反应
And the photons on the other end instantly react.

549
00:30:52,080 --> 00:30:56,320
看上去没有东西移动过，没有能量交换
Nothing seems to move,and no energy is exchanged.

550
00:30:56,320 --> 00:31:01,920
然而，粒子以某种方法 共享信息
Yet somehow,the particles share information.

551
00:31:01,920 --> 00:31:05,360
爱因斯坦称之为 “跨越距离的幽灵反应”
Einstein used the word "spooky action at a distance."

552
00:31:05,360 --> 00:31:07,830
跨越距离的幽灵反应
Sohis spooky action at a distance

553
00:31:07,830 --> 00:31:10,800
并不是在时空传播
is not something that travels in space-time.

554
00:31:10,800 --> 00:31:13,700
它不是在时空中发生的
It's not something that happens in space-time.

555
00:31:13,700 --> 00:31:15,540
没有时空理论能够解释
There's no story in space-time

556
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:18,970
这种非定域性怎么发生的
that can tell us how these nonlocal correlations happen,

557
00:31:18,970 --> 00:31:21,180
我们可以得出结论
and that's why we conclude

558
00:31:21,180 --> 00:31:25,880
非定域性源于时空之外
that they seem to emerge somehow from outside space-time.

559
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:29,020
于是，必然的，这种情况
So that has,of course,deep implication

560
00:31:29,020 --> 00:31:31,820
影响了我们对时空的理解
for our understanding of space-time

561
00:31:31,820 --> 00:31:34,220
实际上，更精确的说
or actually,more precisely,

562
00:31:34,220 --> 00:31:37,760
影响了我们对时空的不理解
for our non-understanding of space-time.

563
00:31:40,230 --> 00:31:43,160
弗里曼:有些人相信 量子非定域性
Freeman:Some believe that quantum nonlocality

564
00:31:43,170 --> 00:31:47,100
能够用于向过去发送信息
can be used to send messages backward in time.

565
00:31:50,670 --> 00:31:52,940
在华盛顿大学
At the University of Washington,

566
00:31:52,940 --> 00:31:56,840
物理学家John Cramer正在 验证这一理论
physicist John Cramer is putting this idea to the test.

567
00:31:56,850 --> 00:32:01,820
和Gisin相似，他也用处于 缠绕态的光子—
Like Gisin,he's experimenting with entangled photons --

568
00:32:01,820 --> 00:32:05,320
利用非定域性绑定的光子对 进行试验
photons bound by nonlocality.

569
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:09,120
不同的是，Cramer试图将光子信号
The twist is that Cramer is trying to send photon signals

570
00:32:09,120 --> 00:32:12,330
从当前传递到非常近的过去
from the present back to the very recent past.

571
00:32:14,100 --> 00:32:16,900
这些定制的激光和测量设备
These custom-made lasers and measuring devices,

572
00:32:16,900 --> 00:32:18,300
叫做干涉仪
called interferometers,

573
00:32:18,300 --> 00:32:21,340
是Cramer的时间机器的核心
are the heart of Cramer's time machine.

574
00:32:21,340 --> 00:32:23,600
一个干涉仪叫做Alice
One interferometer called "Alice"

575
00:32:23,610 --> 00:32:28,880
将光子信号传给另一个叫 Bob的干涉仪
sends photon signals to another interferometer called "Bob."

576
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:30,750
如果Cramer的理论是正确的
If Cramer's theory is correct

577
00:32:30,750 --> 00:32:33,080
仪器的标定也没有问题
and the calibration is just right,

578
00:32:33,080 --> 00:32:36,320
Bob会在Alice发消息的 很短时间之前
Bob will get a message from Alice

579
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:40,290
就收到这个消息
a fraction of a second before she sends it.

580
00:32:40,290 --> 00:32:43,620
因与果要颠倒了
Cause and effect will be reversed.

581
00:32:43,630 --> 00:32:44,790
Alice控制
So Alice has control

582
00:32:44,790 --> 00:32:47,260
我们观察到粒子相
over whether we have particle-like behavior

583
00:32:47,260 --> 00:32:49,930
或者波动相
or wavelike behavior over here.

584
00:32:49,930 --> 00:32:53,170
因为光子纠缠于空间中
Because the photons are entangled in space,

585
00:32:53,170 --> 00:32:56,100
Bob，在那边接受信号
Bob,who wants to receive the signal over here,

586
00:32:56,100 --> 00:32:57,440
可以观察并看到
can look and see

587
00:32:57,440 --> 00:33:00,610
它是否同时具有干涉模式
whether he has an interference pattern at the same time.

588
00:33:00,610 --> 00:33:04,950
现在，这个距离是几厘米
Now,this distance is a few centimeters.

589
00:33:04,950 --> 00:33:06,080
并不大
It's not very big.

590
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:08,150
但是距离不一定要是几厘米
But it doesn't have to be a few centimeters.

591
00:33:08,150 --> 00:33:10,250
也可以是上光年的距离
This could be a light-year down the line,

592
00:33:10,250 --> 00:33:12,150
试验的结果
and she could still do the same thing

593
00:33:12,150 --> 00:33:14,060
不会有什么不同
and cause the same effect over here.

594
00:33:14,060 --> 00:33:16,920
这是纠缠态的工作方式
And that's the way entanglement works.

595
00:33:16,930 --> 00:33:20,360
如果我在这里放一卷光纤
And so if I put a spool of fiber optics in here

596
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:25,470
有10千米长，Alice会在Bob接到信号
that's,say,10 kilometers long,then she would send the signal

597
00:33:25,470 --> 00:33:27,870
之后50微秒发射信号
50 microseconds after Bob received it.

598
00:33:27,870 --> 00:33:30,870
这样她就向50微秒以前的世界
So she would be sending messages backwards in time

599
00:33:30,870 --> 00:33:32,340
发射消息
by 50 microseconds.

600
00:33:32,340 --> 00:33:34,780
这样，理论上
So one could use it,in principle,

601
00:33:34,780 --> 00:33:37,340
某人可以用它实现 与过去通信
for backwards-in-time communication.

602
00:33:39,980 --> 00:33:43,180
弗里曼:如果Cramer的装置正常工作
Freeman:If Cramer's device works,

603
00:33:43,190 --> 00:33:45,350
它会在信息发射之前就发射信息
it will only send messages back

604
00:33:45,350 --> 00:33:48,190
虽然只是百万分之一秒之前
a millionth of a second before they're sent,

605
00:33:48,190 --> 00:33:51,630
但是一个出现在过去的信号
but a signal showing itself even a tiny bit in the past

606
00:33:51,630 --> 00:33:54,730
哪怕再微小，也将给我们的时间观 带来革命性的改变
would revolutionize our understanding of time.

607
00:33:57,030 --> 00:33:59,970
这会证明，逆因果律是真实的
It would prove that retrocausality,

608
00:33:59,970 --> 00:34:02,970
即未来事件会影响过去
the theory that events in the future

609
00:34:02,970 --> 00:34:06,940
这个理论是真实的
affect events in the past,is true.

610
00:34:06,940 --> 00:34:10,780
Cramer:如果它真的起作用了 那会是很有意义的
Cramer:If it does work,it would be quite remarkable,

611
00:34:10,780 --> 00:34:12,650
是物理学的大事件
be a big deal in physics.

612
00:34:12,650 --> 00:34:16,520
是信息工程的大事件
It would be a big deal in the communication industry.

613
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:18,620
如果你能向过去发送消息
And if you could send messages backwards in time,

614
00:34:18,620 --> 00:34:20,150
这对一切来说都是大事件
it would be a big deal everywhere.

615
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:21,760
这会改变我们的文明
It would change our civilization

616
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:23,560
我都无法设想会发生什么
in ways I have trouble imagining.

617
00:34:23,560 --> 00:34:26,030
但是这也许是个迹象
But all of that is probably just an indication

618
00:34:26,030 --> 00:34:28,230
这个试验恐怕不会成功
that the experiment probably won't work,

619
00:34:28,230 --> 00:34:30,830
因为自然恐怕不会允许人类
because nature probably doesn't want to allow you

620
00:34:30,830 --> 00:34:32,770
向过去发送信息
to send messages backwards in time.

621
00:34:34,870 --> 00:34:37,270
我并不真的认为
I don't really see retrocausality

622
00:34:37,270 --> 00:34:39,340
逆因果律是一个很可信的假设
as a very plausible assumption.

623
00:34:39,340 --> 00:34:44,110
我是说，很明显，时间向着未来演化
I mean,time clearly evolves or gets constructed

624
00:34:44,110 --> 00:34:45,480
或者说构造着未来
towards the future.

625
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:47,920
另一方面，我也会说
On the other side,I will also say

626
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:51,520
对现代的物理学家和物理学理论
that time is certainly a very poorly understood concept

627
00:34:51,520 --> 00:34:53,560
时间是一个很不被理解的概念
in physics by physicists today,

628
00:34:53,560 --> 00:34:56,730
我们应该期望，在未来
and one can certainly expect that in the future

629
00:34:56,730 --> 00:34:59,660
我们能够更好和更深刻的理解时间
we'll have a much better and deeper understanding of time

630
00:34:59,660 --> 00:35:02,730
和今日的理解大不相同
and possibly a very different one from the one we have today.

631
00:35:10,340 --> 00:35:12,210
让我们说，总有一天
So let's say that someday

632
00:35:12,210 --> 00:35:15,480
我们发展了更好的时间观
we develop that better understanding of time.

633
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:18,780
在解决了量子引力之谜后
After solving the riddle of quantum gravity,

634
00:35:18,780 --> 00:35:21,050
我们建造一个能用的时间机器
we build a working time machine.

635
00:35:21,050 --> 00:35:23,890
那会发生什么事呢？
What would happen then?

636
00:35:23,890 --> 00:35:28,460
我们能够改变过去吗？
Would we be able to change the past?

637
00:35:28,460 --> 00:35:34,630
这个答案很炫，也很恼人
The answers are fantastic,disturbing,

638
00:35:34,630 --> 00:35:36,970
还有一点
and a little...

639
00:35:38,800 --> 00:35:41,470
...怪异...
...Strange...

640
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:48,860
我们试图向过去发信号
We're trying to send signals back in time.

641
00:35:48,860 --> 00:35:50,330
如果成功，
And if that works,

642
00:35:50,330 --> 00:35:54,030
也许有一天 我们能把人送回过去
perhaps one day we can send humans back in time.

643
00:35:54,030 --> 00:35:55,570
一个令人激动的想法
An exciting idea,

644
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:59,570
但它开启了一扇悖论问题的大门
but it opens the door to the problem of paradox.

645
00:35:59,570 --> 00:36:03,980
悖论是一个自相矛盾的情况
A paradox is a situation that contradicts itself --

646
00:36:03,980 --> 00:36:06,040
悖论本身不合情理
doesn't make any sense.

647
00:36:06,050 --> 00:36:11,050
你从未来向过去发送一个 治疗癌症的药方
Say you send a cure for cancer from the future to the past.

648
00:36:11,050 --> 00:36:13,550
现在的死人会活吗？
Would the dead now be alive?

649
00:36:13,550 --> 00:36:14,920
明白了？
See?

650
00:36:14,920 --> 00:36:17,720
时间旅行充满了这样的奥秘
Time travel is filled with such mysteries.

651
00:36:24,030 --> 00:36:28,030
关于时间旅行，我们所关心的
The things we would like to understand about time travel

652
00:36:28,030 --> 00:36:31,270
其中一点是，原理上是否可行
are,one,is it possible,even in principle,

653
00:36:31,270 --> 00:36:35,070
物理定律是否允许 回到过去的时间旅行
that the laws of physics permit backward time travel?

654
00:36:35,070 --> 00:36:37,540
我们不知道答案
We don't know the answer.

655
00:36:37,540 --> 00:36:39,410
为了找到答案
We need the laws of quantum gravity

656
00:36:39,410 --> 00:36:41,010
我们需要量子引力定律
in order to find out the answer.

657
00:36:41,010 --> 00:36:45,280
第二个问题是，如果有可能进行 回到过去的时间旅行
Second question is,if backward time travel is possible,

658
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:48,150
那么，自然会对所谓的
then what does nature do

659
00:36:48,150 --> 00:36:51,290
祖父悖论作何反应
about the so-called grandfather paradox,

660
00:36:51,290 --> 00:36:55,230
祖父悖论是说，我回到过去
that I can go backward in time if it's possible

661
00:36:55,230 --> 00:36:59,730
在我老爹还是两个细胞，分居两地时，
就把他老爹，我爷爷干掉了
and kill my grandfather before my father was conceived,

662
00:36:59,730 --> 00:37:04,570
由此历史改变了 于是我就不存在了？
thereby changing history so that I no longer exist?

663
00:37:04,570 --> 00:37:06,740
自然会对此作何反应呢？
What does nature do about that?

664
00:37:08,170 --> 00:37:11,440
Gott:保守的解释是
Gott:The conservative interpretation

665
00:37:11,440 --> 00:37:15,010
时空是四维的存在
is that space-time is one four-dimensional thing.

666
00:37:15,010 --> 00:37:16,450
是不会改变滴
It doesn't change.

667
00:37:16,450 --> 00:37:19,650
因此如果时间旅行者 返回过去
So if time travelers go to the past,

668
00:37:19,650 --> 00:37:24,520
他们就永远是过去的一部分，他们没有改变时空
they were always part of the past,and they don't change it.

669
00:37:24,520 --> 00:37:28,890
换句话说，如果时间旅行者 登上 泰坦尼克号,
In other words,if you had time travelers aboard the Titanic,

670
00:37:28,890 --> 00:37:31,730
他们警告船长，有冰山
they might have warned the Captain about the iceberg,

671
00:37:31,730 --> 00:37:33,970
但船长根本不会在意
but he didn't pay any attention to them,

672
00:37:33,970 --> 00:37:37,040
就像他对其他的冰山警告 也不在意一样
like he didn't pay any attention to the other iceberg warnings,

673
00:37:37,040 --> 00:37:40,300
因为我们知道这倒霉催的船 最后撞上了冰山
because we know the ship ended up hitting an iceberg.

674
00:37:40,310 --> 00:37:42,270
于是保守观点认为
So that's the conservative view,

675
00:37:42,270 --> 00:37:45,580
时间旅行者没有改变历史
that time travelers don't alter the past.

676
00:37:45,580 --> 00:37:48,350
他们能够参与历史
They can participate in the past.

677
00:37:48,350 --> 00:37:50,380
实际上，一个小丑曾经说过
In fact,one wag once said

678
00:37:50,380 --> 00:37:52,680
泰坦尼克沉没的真正原因
that the real thing that sank the Titanic

679
00:37:52,690 --> 00:37:56,390
是因为好事的时间旅行者太多了 他们跑上去，把船压沉了
was the extra weight of all the stowaway time travelers

680
00:37:56,390 --> 00:38:00,190
[ 笑 ] 登船观赏沉没
[ laughing ] Onboard to see it sink.

681
00:38:00,190 --> 00:38:04,630
弗里曼:实际上，我们为什么没有被
来自未来的时间旅客所环绕？
Freeman:In fact,there's a simple reason we aren't surrounded

682
00:38:04,630 --> 00:38:07,730
有一个简单的原因
by time-traveling tourists from the future.

683
00:38:07,730 --> 00:38:11,470
那就是没有人能够制造出 管用的时间机器来
It's because no one has built a working time machine.

684
00:38:14,110 --> 00:38:15,710
即使某一天
Even if we someday

685
00:38:15,710 --> 00:38:19,210
我们拥有 能够回到过去的科技
have the technology to travel back in time,

686
00:38:19,210 --> 00:38:21,310
时间机器将只会在
the machine will only work

687
00:38:21,310 --> 00:38:24,320
我们发明它的那一刻启动
starting at the point we invent it,

688
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:26,820
创造出时间回路
creating the first loop in time.

689
00:38:26,820 --> 00:38:29,120
当你在公元3000年，
When you create a time machine

690
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:32,690
通过移动宇宙弦创造出 时间机器时
by moving cosmic strings up in the year 3000,

691
00:38:32,690 --> 00:38:36,060
你在公元3000年 通过扭曲时间和空间
you create a time loop up in the year 3000

692
00:38:36,060 --> 00:38:38,160
创造了时间回路
by twisting space and time.

693
00:38:38,160 --> 00:38:40,430
当时间旅客出发
So when the time traveler goes,

694
00:38:40,430 --> 00:38:44,000
他向未来前进，像这辆车
he goes always toward the future,like this car.

695
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:45,670
他沿着回路前进
He goes around the loop,

696
00:38:45,670 --> 00:38:49,540
那意味着他能从3002年
and that means that he can go from the year 3002

697
00:38:49,540 --> 00:38:51,540
回到3001年
back to the year 3001,

698
00:38:51,540 --> 00:38:54,910
但他不能回到2010年
but he can't come back here to 2010,

699
00:38:54,910 --> 00:38:58,980
因为那是在 时间机器建造之前
because that's before the time machine was built.

700
00:38:58,980 --> 00:39:04,190
弗里曼:但也许有一个例外
Freeman:But there may be an exception to these rules.

701
00:39:04,190 --> 00:39:05,860
又一次
And,once again,

702
00:39:05,860 --> 00:39:10,030
它超出了量子力学的奇怪世界
it grows out of the weird world of quantum mechanics.

703
00:39:10,030 --> 00:39:12,300
许多量子物理学家相信
Many quantum physicists believe

704
00:39:12,300 --> 00:39:16,270
具有无数的平行宇宙
there is an incalculable number of parallel universes,

705
00:39:16,270 --> 00:39:21,210
这些平行宇宙围绕着我们
and these parallel universes are all around us.

706
00:39:21,210 --> 00:39:24,310
在量子力学的 多重世界理论里
Every time you make a decision that could have gone

707
00:39:24,310 --> 00:39:27,580
每次你做出一个决断，
one way or the other -- you flip a coin,for example --

708
00:39:27,580 --> 00:39:30,110
决定走这条路或者那一条— 比如，扔一个硬币—
it could have gone the other way,

709
00:39:30,120 --> 00:39:32,080
可能会出现两种情况
and then the universe would branch off

710
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:33,580
于是宇宙就开枝散叶
into two separate branches

711
00:39:33,590 --> 00:39:35,590
变成2根分离的枝条
in the many-worlds theory of quantum mechanics.

712
00:39:35,590 --> 00:39:37,960
Carroll:如果你承认多重宇宙
Carroll:If you allow for alternate universes,

713
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:39,490
那么很多事就可能发生
then lots of things can happen.

714
00:39:39,490 --> 00:39:42,360
你也可以避免逻辑悖论的产生
It's still true that you have to avoid logical paradoxes.

715
00:39:42,360 --> 00:39:44,730
所有发生的事也真的发生了
It's still true that what happened did happen,

716
00:39:44,730 --> 00:39:47,130
但那只意味着是在 一个宇宙中发生
but it means that what happened in one universe

717
00:39:47,130 --> 00:39:48,470
在那个 宇宙发生
happened in that universe.

718
00:39:48,470 --> 00:39:51,240
变化并不影响新宇宙
It doesn't apply to the new universe.

719
00:39:54,510 --> 00:39:56,240
如果按照量子力学的理论
If the many worlds exist,

720
00:39:56,240 --> 00:39:59,410
存在很多个世界
which they do,according to quantum mechanics,

721
00:39:59,410 --> 00:40:00,950
如果你回到过去
then what you would do

722
00:40:00,950 --> 00:40:03,920
干掉了你那不幸的爷爷
is you go back to kill your grandfather,

723
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:08,450
那是一个和你爷爷完全相同的人
you kill a man who is identical to your grandfather,

724
00:40:08,450 --> 00:40:12,490
但他只在平行世界里是你的爷爷
but he is only your grandfather in a parallel world.

725
00:40:12,490 --> 00:40:14,160
在那个平行世界里
In that parallel world,

726
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:18,130
你的爷爷被 来自另一个宇宙的你所杀
your grandfather being killed by you from another universe

727
00:40:18,130 --> 00:40:22,030
不再会生儿育女，包括你
is never going to give rise to your father,hence to you.

728
00:40:22,030 --> 00:40:23,640
但是没问题
But that's no problem,

729
00:40:23,640 --> 00:40:27,240
因为你在那个宇宙里 从来就没存在过
because you have never existed at all in this universe.

730
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:32,310
你乘时间机器所做的 不过是穿行宇宙
What you've done in your time machine is cross the universes.

731
00:40:34,180 --> 00:40:37,650
弗里曼:但是看上去
Freeman:But there seems to be little chance

732
00:40:37,650 --> 00:40:40,090
短期内，时间旅客
of time traveling anytime soon,

733
00:40:40,090 --> 00:40:44,160
没什么机会进入存在的过去 或者平行宇宙
either into the existing past or a parallel universe.

734
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:49,260
我们的科技水平
The technology that would be required to make a time machine

735
00:40:49,260 --> 00:40:53,200
距离制造时间机器还非常遥远
that has even a whisper of a hope of success

736
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:55,670
我们与时间机器之间的差距
is as far beyond us today

737
00:40:55,670 --> 00:40:59,040
和变形虫与星际旅行之间 的差距差不多
as space travel is beyond the capabilities of an amoeba,

738
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:03,840
我们的技术太微不足道了
because our technology is so puny.

739
00:41:03,840 --> 00:41:05,510
根本就没戏
There's no hope at all.

740
00:41:08,280 --> 00:41:12,820
弗里曼:如果我们致力于把
Freeman:Time travel seems unlikely if we approach it purely as a matter

741
00:41:12,820 --> 00:41:15,950
一个人或者信息从现在 传输到过去
of taking a person or information from the present

742
00:41:15,960 --> 00:41:17,920
这种时间旅行看起来不大可能
and transporting it to the past.

743
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:21,290
但有另一个办法能够 回到过去
But there is another way to journey into the past,

744
00:41:21,290 --> 00:41:23,030
一个直到最近
a way that until recently

745
00:41:23,030 --> 00:41:25,760
还被人当笑话讲
would have been considered preposterous

746
00:41:25,770 --> 00:41:29,300
但是每天都越来越接近现实
but is getting closer to reality every day.

747
00:41:29,300 --> 00:41:33,170
我们能够建造 过去
We could build the past.

748
00:41:33,170 --> 00:41:37,010
人类科技以指数速度进化
Human technology is evolving exponentially.

749
00:41:37,010 --> 00:41:39,540
当我们的电脑足够强大
When our computers get powerful enough,

750
00:41:39,550 --> 00:41:43,320
它们能够仿真 非常复杂的世界
they could simulate massively complex worlds,

751
00:41:43,320 --> 00:41:46,520
包括过去的地球
including past eras of life on Earth.

752
00:41:46,520 --> 00:41:51,260
这可不是电子游戏
These wouldn't be video games.

753
00:41:51,260 --> 00:41:55,790
对过去的仿真足以 以假乱真
These simulations of the past would look and feel so real,

754
00:41:55,800 --> 00:41:59,160
你不会发现这是冒牌的—
you wouldn't know they are simulations --

755
00:41:59,170 --> 00:42:03,640
不是真实的过去 只是仅次于真实的模拟
not the genuine past,but the next-best thing.

756
00:42:03,640 --> 00:42:06,770
Tipler:如果你真的想回到过去
Tipler:If you really want to go into the past,

757
00:42:06,770 --> 00:42:10,380
你将必须回到非常遥远的过去
you're going to have to go into the extreme far future.

758
00:42:10,380 --> 00:42:12,110
在非常遥远的过去
In the extreme far future,

759
00:42:12,110 --> 00:42:16,750
他们会有能力重建过去
they will have the ability to reproduce the past.

760
00:42:16,750 --> 00:42:20,020
你就能亲眼看到 过去是什么样
And then you can see what the past was like.

761
00:42:20,020 --> 00:42:23,290
你能通过在虚拟现实中的存在
You can actually experience the distant past

762
00:42:23,290 --> 00:42:25,920
真正体验遥远的过去
by existing in the virtual reality

763
00:42:25,930 --> 00:42:28,590
遥远未来的计算机实现这一切
of the computers of the far future.

764
00:42:45,880 --> 00:42:50,820
我们看到，实现到遥远未来 的旅行是可能的
We've seen that time travel into the distant future is possible.

765
00:42:50,820 --> 00:42:52,780
但却是有去无回
But it's a one-way trip.

766
00:42:52,790 --> 00:42:57,760
回到过去理论上是 有可能的
Time travel into the past might be theoretically possible,

767
00:42:57,760 --> 00:43:01,890
但那需要难以想象 的巨大能量
but it requires inconceivable amounts of energy

768
00:43:01,890 --> 00:43:04,030
以及神一般的科技
and god-like technology.

769
00:43:04,030 --> 00:43:06,330
我们最乐观的希望
Our best hope may lie

770
00:43:06,330 --> 00:43:10,570
也许是由计算机重建过去
in computer re-creations of times past.

771
00:43:10,570 --> 00:43:14,340
所以看上去我们不太可能 回到过去
So it looks like we won't be able to go back in time

772
00:43:14,340 --> 00:43:16,740
去和我们失去的人碰面
to visit the people we've lost

773
00:43:16,740 --> 00:43:21,210
或者纠正年轻时犯下的错误
or correct the mistakes we made when we were young.

774
00:43:21,210 --> 00:43:26,850
我们穿越时间的轨迹，从生到死
Our trajectory through time,from birth to death,

775
00:43:26,850 --> 00:43:30,160
是所有生命的共同点
is the one thing all living things have in common.

776
00:43:30,160 --> 00:43:32,720
每个人都要 接受这样的现实
Every human has to live with the fact

777
00:43:32,730 --> 00:43:36,660
人生苦短，光阴宝贵
that life is short and time is precious.

778
00:43:36,660 --> 00:43:40,870
我们有光辉岁月 我们也会有千古之恨
We have our triumphs. We make our mistakes.

779
00:43:40,870 --> 00:43:44,570
如果我们能够回到过去 纠正错误
If we could go back and correct those mistakes,

780
00:43:44,570 --> 00:43:47,740
我们会从中吸取教训吗？
would we ever learn anything from them?

781
00:43:47,740 --> 00:43:51,440
我们还会是今天的我们吗？
Would we be the people we are today?

782
00:43:51,440 --> 00:43:55,450
现在，至少，我们还无法回拨时间
For now,at least,we can't turn back the clock.

783
00:43:55,450 --> 00:43:59,150
但...我们会一直尝试的
But...We'll keep trying.

784
00:43:59,150 --> 00:44:02,650
一直尝试
We will keep trying.

785
00:44:02,660 --> 00:44:05,560
-- 感谢观赏 --

